<!--
    kuna lanefuse: P2 flow, option lanefuse on|all|off (default on).

      0x1000 addv:    vaddps ymm0,ymm0,ymm1; ret                  (VEX, eight float lanes)
      0x1010 madd:    kmovw k1,edi; vaddps zmm0{k1},zmm1,zmm2; ret        (EVEX merge mask)
      0x1020 maddz:   kmovw k1,edi; vaddps zmm0{k1}{z},zmm0,zmm1; ret     (EVEX zero mask)
      0x1030 add128:  addps xmm0,xmm1; ret                        (legacy SSE, four float lanes)
      0x1040 add128i: paddd xmm0,xmm1; ret                        (legacy SSE, integer lanes)
      0x1050 mul128d: mulpd xmm0,xmm1; ret                        (legacy SSE, two double lanes)

    The SLEIGH spec writes these instructions lane by lane, and applies an
    AVX-512 write mask as a multiply-or per lane after the user-op.

    The first pass is `lanefuse off`, the second the default, the third
    `lanefuse all` on the two legacy-SSE shapes the default leaves as lanes.
-->
